    {
      "id": "oe_8zn19SdZSaPdfE-qWE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 966.6877155549112,
      "y": 153.22219817976574,
      "width": 1102.6956787109375,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b06",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1017298087,
      "version": 1566,
      "versionNonce": 1756210729,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "Gs8oMW1iQhZy2vYOBry8Y",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1787435916149,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nworkspace\n \n- Repos: They can be symlinks to the canonical / read-only version \n    - workspace itself can be SCM, but when used, they needs to be \"rehydrated\"\n- Repo's worktrees \n    - we should manage their lifecycle as we start / complete a task\n    - it should align more with \"execution-notes\" instead of workspace itself. \n- Symlinks to execution folder\n    - so that we know active projects under a workspace \n- Inbox: unstructured contents, require further process, scratch pad, etc. \n    - e.g. raw paper to read etc. \n- context: processed contents, usually from inbox, not-repo\n    - e.g. paper's discussion notes, actions yield etc. \n- sidecars: actions in workspace level\n    - defined workflow in workspace. e.g. Concepts learning, 3rd app push ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nworkspace\n \n- Repos: They can be symlinks to the canonical / read-only version \n    - workspace itself can be SCM, but when used, they needs to be \"rehydrated\"\n- Repo's worktrees \n    - we should manage their lifecycle as we start / complete a task\n    - it should align more with \"execution-notes\" instead of workspace itself. \n- Symlinks to execution folder\n    - so that we know active projects under a workspace \n- Inbox: unstructured contents, require further process, scratch pad, etc. \n    - e.g. raw paper to read etc. \n- context: processed contents, usually from inbox, not-repo\n    - e.g. paper's discussion notes, actions yield etc. \n- sidecars: actions in workspace level\n    - defined workflow in workspace. e.g. Concepts learning, 3rd app push ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
