      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"workspace is the factory, task folders are warehouse\"\n\"Ideally you shouldn't need to build too many factories, but as you scale, you need more\" ",
      "fontSize": 27.29002178089706,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"workspace is the factory, task folders are warehouse\"\n\"Ideally you shouldn't need to build too many factories, but as you scale, you need more\" ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YNUItS1x4d8LROl0yrieg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 57.351953112921876,
      "y": 1181.2125045278476,
      "width": 1534.483154296875,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 400575945,
      "version": 742,
      "versionNonce": 777569703,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787438513784,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Gaps to fill\n- Initialize task within workspace should have a established process:\n    - creating a subfolder in execution-notes \n    - register tmux session through tss so it can be discovered \n    - register into tack as a ongoing tasks \n- Initialize workspace lacks things like inbox, context and sidecars\n- Clarify agent-tasks is kind of mixing workspace and executuon-notes all together, but agent-workspace is for \nreusable workspace and different tasks, and it generate enough artifacts to warrant its separate space. the \npure agent-task initialization is for nimble things suitable for daily life. ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Gaps to fill\n- Initialize task within workspace should have a established process:\n    - creating a subfolder in execution-notes \n    - register tmux session through tss so it can be discovered \n    - register into tack as a ongoing tasks \n- Initialize workspace lacks things like inbox, context and sidecars\n- Clarify agent-tasks is kind of mixing workspace and executuon-notes all together, but agent-workspace is for \nreusable workspace and different tasks, and it generate enough artifacts to warrant its separate space. the \npure agent-task initialization is for nimble things suitable for daily life. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
